      "writtenOn": "2023-11-10T19:14:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is intended to be passive, in the sense that FAFT just watches for things it expects. If the FAFT tests need to issue an EC command then it becomes less useful. In particular it makes it hard to deal with reboots, where we want to wait for the dev screen to come up. With the current design, this is quite easy.",
      "parentUuid": "85904c08_f0e9b391",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "a79da8e697548ff3a621a8db0f01db931c2c54de",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb7e8c61_cfebda16",
        "filename": "common/host_command.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T19:24:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My suggestion is to do both.  The EC prints out the AP_FW state as it is received from the AP and provide a console command to print out the last AP_FW state received.\n\nThe console command can be used by FAFT if polling for the desired state fails.  Parsing console output is fragile, so the console command gives  FAFT a chance to retry.",
      "parentUuid": "ed594f5a_7e631a2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 270,
